{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121133","id":4021803725,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7vt9rN","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121133","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121133.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121133.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121133","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121133/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121133/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121133/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/9adfd25b2ede00e4b791af0ca54047d027fd61b2","number":121133,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Show a proper error for the invalid \"..\" operator","user":{"login":"Chaganti-Reddy","id":97330178,"node_id":"U_kgDOBc0kAg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97330178?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaganti-Reddy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\n\n- Closes #96003\n\nif you accidentally type `..` instead of `.` in an expression, like `obj..method()`, gdscript throws a misleading error that points at the wrong place (e.g. `Expected \":\" after \"if\" condition`). the reason is `..` (the `PERIOD_PERIOD` token) has no infix rule in the expression parser, so the parser just stops there and leaves the stray `..` sitting unconsumed. then whatever demands a token next (the colon after the if here) is what complains, so the error blames the colon instead of the actual `..`.\n\n## Additional information\n\ngave `PERIOD_PERIOD` an infix handler in the parser rules table that reports `Unexpected \"..\", did you mean \".\"?` and then recovers by treating it as a single `.`, so you get one clear error instead of the misleading one.\n\nthis only touches expressions - the valid `..` rest pattern in `match` goes through a separate code path, so it is untouched (checked it still parses fine). also confirmed normal `.` access still works. added a parser regression test at `parser/errors/double_dot`.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labe